From 4ddeccabd5a2901539d56879a49be8a837b1b41f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 22:21:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add automint: free public NFT mint watcher and executor

Watches for NFT collections that just went live and mints the genuinely
free public ones from a burner wallet.

The core design constraint is that every transaction has value: 0. That
makes "is this mint free?" a question the chain answers rather than a
marketplace API: candidate mint routes are probed through eth_estimateGas
with zero value, so anything that actually charges reverts and is
discarded. It also means no approval is ever signed and no externally
supplied calldata is ever sent, which removes the usual "free mint"
drain vectors.

Pipeline:
- discovery: sweeps recent blocks for Transfer/TransferSingle from
  address(0) to catch mints as they happen, plus an optional OpenSea
  API adapter for newly created collections
- screening: ERC-165/behavioural standard detection, mint-route probing
  across ~15 known signatures including SeaDrop and thirdweb, gas
  budget checks, and an eth_simulateV1 check that a token actually
  transfers to us
- execution: capped priority fee, gas buffer over estimate, receipt
  confirmation, outcome persisted

Safety defaults: dry run on unless explicitly disabled, per-mint and
per-day-per-chain gas ceilings, deny/allow lists, a kill-switch file
checked before every mint, and one attempt per contract.

Chains are config-driven, so adding one is a config edit. Tests use a
local JSON-RPC mock node, so the integration suite exercises the real
viem client path end to end without network access.

